  "answer": "The recurring onboarding blockers are:\n\n1. **Permission mapping / RBAC synchronization** – the most common blocker, caused by replicating customers' Active Directory or folder permission structures into NovaLearn; nested/circular group configurations can halt directory mirroring [NL-031#NL-031-S04] [NL-005#NL-005-S06]. It accounts for 45% of onboarding delays [NL-031#NL-031-S04] [NL-012#NL-012-S06].\n\n2. **Source ingestion cleanup** – outdated, redundant, or corrupted files must be removed before indexing; customers often dump un-reviewed folders into KnowledgeHub, pausing onboarding while manuals cleanup occurs [NL-031#NL-031-S04]. It accounts for 30% of delays [NL-031#NL-031-S04] [NL-012#NL-012-S06].\n\n3. **OCR / scanned PDF processing** – image-only legacy PDFs return incomplete citations because the standard parser fails to detect text layers, failing the go-live citation threshold [NL-031#NL-031-S04]. It accounts for 25% of delays [NL-031#NL-031-S04] [NL-012#NL-012-S06]. Enterprise onboarding is also frequently delayed by security reviews, SSO setups, custom data-retention configurations, and scanned PDF policy OCR [NL-005#NL-005-S02] [NL-012#NL-012-S06].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
